From: Mateusz Krawczuk <mateusz.krawczuk@cybrixsystems.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Apr 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: tegra194: add nvidia-nvrm node for NVRM

The NVIDIA out-of-tree nvidia.ko driver (from nvdisplay) requires a
device tree node with compatible = "nvidia,tegra194-nvrm" to probe
as a platform device. On Xavier, nvidia.ko serves as NVRM resource
manager only (display is handled by tegra-drm.ko). Uses a unique
compatible string to avoid conflict with tegra-display-hub which
claims "nvidia,tegra194-display".

The nvidia,disp-sw-soc-chip-id property encodes the HIDREV register
value: CHIPID=0x19 in bits[15:8], MAJORREV=0x4 in bits[7:4], giving
the raw value 0x1940. The driver computes:
  hidrev = (CHIPID << 4) | MAJORREV = 0x194

This is a minimal node with no MMIO regions or interrupts since display
hardware is managed by tegra-drm.ko.

Signed-off-by: Mateusz Krawczuk <mateusz.krawczuk@cybrixsystems.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra194.dtsi | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra194.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra194.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra194.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra194.dtsi
@@ -3186,4 +3186,10 @@
 		compatible = "nvidia,carveouts-t19x";
 		status = "okay";
 	};
+
+	nvidia-nvrm {
+		compatible = "nvidia,tegra194-nvrm";
+		nvidia,disp-sw-soc-chip-id = <0x1940>;
+		status = "okay";
+	};
 };
